invariant: INV-14
file: handshake_parser.c
catches: handshake_strict_webpki
reason: a TRUST=webpki server_name acknowledgement that carries data
  still fails, but with unsupported_extension, the alert for an
  extension the client never offered, instead of decode_error, the
  alert RFC 9846 §6 names for a body of the wrong length. The client
  offered server_name, so the wire alert would name the wrong fault.
  bin/handshake_strict_webpki's server_name alert rows object.

--- old
    return ext == EXT_SERVER_NAME ? ALERT_DECODE_ERROR : ALERT_UNSUPPORTED_EXTENSION;
--- new
    (void)ext;
    return ALERT_UNSUPPORTED_EXTENSION;
